#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tkmusic - search and play music from many places, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only for the program itself; playback is done by mpv, and
YouTube / YouTube Music / SoundCloud audio is fetched with yt-dlp (the newest
yt-dlp found on the PATH or in Homebrew is used).

Sources:
  YouTube Music     song search (YouTube Music's own search API)
  YouTube           video search via yt-dlp
  SoundCloud        track search via yt-dlp
  Bandcamp          artists / albums / tracks (full streams where the artist
                    allows it)
  Internet Archive  live recordings, netlabels, old 78s ...
  Radio             ~50,000 internet radio stations (radio-browser.info)
  Spotify           search only: Spotify does not allow other programs to
                    stream its audio, so a Spotify track is played from
                    YouTube Music (or opened in the Spotify app/web player).
                    Needs a free API key from developer.spotify.com, set as
                    spotify_client_id / spotify_client_secret in
                    ~/.tkmusic.json or SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID / _SECRET.
  A URL typed into the search box is played directly (or opened, for
  Bandcamp and Internet Archive pages).

Searching: the menu next to the source picks the field the words are
matched against (any, artist, album, title or genre), and fields can also
be typed into the search box, as in
    artist:radiohead album:kid a        (also by:, track:, song:, tag:)
Words before the first field go to the field in the menu.  Spotify and the
Internet Archive search fields themselves; YouTube Music, YouTube,
SoundCloud and Bandcamp results are searched for all the words and then
filtered on the field; sources that cannot search a field are skipped
(radio stations only have a genre).

Usage:  tkmusic [search words | audio files / playlists]
        tkmusic --build-app [DIR]    build a macOS tkmusic.app (with icon)
        tkmusic --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]

The app opens audio files and playlists dropped on it or opened from Finder.

Keys:
  Return (search box)   search            Ctrl-F or /   go to search box
  Return / double-click play (albums, artists and archive items open)
  BackSpace             back to the previous list
  A                     add to queue      N   play next
  F                     add to / remove from favourites
  Space                 pause / resume    Ctrl-Left / Ctrl-Right  prev / next
  Delete (queue)        remove from queue
  Right-click           more actions (open web page, copy URL ...)
  Ctrl-Q                quit
"""

